</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The reward function for the driving skill is designed to encourage progress toward the target while promoting stable and purposeful motion. It is defined as</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_left"><math id="A2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}=\begin{cases}c_{d}\Delta d+c_{a}\bigl(1-40\theta^{2}\bigr)-c_{t}-c_{s}(a_{t}-a_{t-1})^{2},&amp;\text{step reward (progress, alignment, smoothness)}\\[6.0pt]
1,&amp;\text{if the rover stops within $4\,\text{m}$ of the target (success)}\\[6.0pt]
-0.5,&amp;\text{if $\theta&gt;30^{\circ}$ (failure, episode terminated)}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>40</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>step reward (progress, alignment, smoothness)</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if the rover stops within </mtext><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>m</mtext></mrow><mtext> of the target (success)</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mn>30</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><mtext> (failure, episode terminated)</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}=\begin{cases}c_{d}\Delta d+c_{a}\bigl(1-40\theta^{2}\bigr)-c_{t}-c_{s}(a_{t}-a_{t-1})^{2},&amp;\text{step reward (progress, alignment, smoothness)}\\[6.0pt]
1,&amp;\text{if the rover stops within $4\,\text{m}$ of the target (success)}\\[6.0pt]
-0.5,&amp;\text{if $\theta&gt;30^{\circ}$ (failure, episode terminated)}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta d</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the change in distance to the target, <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> is the angle between the rover’s heading and the direction to the target, and <math id="A2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the normalized action at time <math id="A2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. The first term rewards forward progress, the second favors alignment with the target direction, the third penalizes idleness, and the last discourages large changes between successive actions. The constants are set to <math id="A2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{d}=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{d}=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{a}=0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{a}=0.02</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t}=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t}=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{s}=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{s}=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">In addition, the rover receives a large terminal reward of <math id="A2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}=1</annotation></semantics></math> when it comes to a stop within <math id="A2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\,\text{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>m</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\,\text{m}</annotation></semantics></math> of the target, signaling successful completion of the task. Conversely, if the heading angle exceeds <math id="A2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="30^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>30</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">30^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>, the episode is terminated early, and a reward of <math id="A2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}=-0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}=-0.5</annotation></semantics></math> is given.</p>
</div>
</section>
</article>
</div>
